{%- comment -%}
  Prints an experience's effective status: upcoming, ongoing or past.

  - "past" in the status field always wins.
  - Otherwise, once the experience's last day (end_date, or start_date when
    there is no end date) is before today, it counts as past, so events move
    to past on their own. An "ongoing" entry without an end date stays ongoing
    until someone sets it to past.

  The status field may be a single choice or a list (for example
  ["Upcoming"]), so it is joined and matched loosely. Dates are compared as
  numbers (YYYYMMDD), not as strings.

  Liquid output is cached, so the calendar and the experience page also check
  the date again in the visitor's browser (see tg-experience-ends).

  Accepts:
  - entry {Object}: an "experience" metaobject entry

  Usage:
  {% capture status %}{% render 'tg-experience-status', entry: entry %}{% endcapture %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign raw = entry.status.value | join: ' ' | downcase | strip
  assign status = 'upcoming'
  if raw contains 'past'
    assign status = 'past'
  elsif raw contains 'ongoing'
    assign status = 'ongoing'
  endif

  if status != 'past'
    assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
    assign last_day = 0
    if entry.end_date.value != blank
      assign last_day = entry.end_date.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
    elsif status == 'upcoming' and entry.start_date.value != blank
      assign last_day = entry.start_date.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
    endif
    if last_day > 0 and last_day < today
      assign status = 'past'
    endif
  endif

  echo status
-%}
